{title: Light of the World}
{subtitle: Matthew 5:14–16}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]You are the light of the [Cm7]world
[Abmaj7]A city on a hill stands [Bb]tall
[Eb]Cannot be hidden from [Ebmaj7/D]the [Cm7]view
No one puts a lamp [Abmaj7]away
They set it on a stand so [Bb]high
It gives [Fm7]light to everyone
In[Bb]side the house of life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let your [Eb]light shine before others
So they [Cm7]see your good works done
And [Ab]glorify your Father
Who is [Bb]seated in heaven
Let your [Eb]light shine before others
See the [Cm7]good works you do
[Ab]Glorify your Father a[Bb]bove
In the bright and end[Eb]less view
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Do not hide beneath [Bb/D]the bas[Cm7]ket
[Ab]No one does this in the [Bb]night
[Eb]Set it on the stand and [Bb/D]stand [Cm7]firm
Let the rays reach every [Ab]soul
In the same way let it [Bb]shine
So they [Fm7]see the truth of you
And [Eb/G]lift their eyes to heaven
Where [Ab]your Father waits for [Bb]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let your [Eb]light shine before others
[Bb/D]So they [Cm7]see your good works done
And [Ab]glorify your Father
Who is [Bb]seated in heaven
Let your [Eb]light shine before others
[Bb/D]See the [Cm7]good works you do
[Ab]Glorify your Father a[Bb]bove
In the bright and end[Eb]less view
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]A city set on a hill
[Bb]Cannot be hidden from [Cm7]sight
Your light is the sign of grace
[Bb/D]That leads us through the day
[Ab]Let it shine for all to [Bb]see
The goodness God has giv[Cm7]en
Glorify the Father in heav[Bb/D]en
With a heart that is for[Ab]given
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Let your [Eb]light shine before others [Cm7]
[Ab]Glorify your Father in [Bb]heaven
{end_of_verse}

